{"agent_id":"pp3g-jXJg-ac-2-reviewer-successfully-reports-findings-e5ed","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-07-27T16:31:34.462436471Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7b0d84e4-7753-40dc-bc53-2fa5ce6b4a7e","comment_uuid":"5e872d28-dc5f-4c1b-83f7-7b40eea07067","author":"pp3g-jXJg-ac-2-reviewer-successfully-reports-findings-e5ed","content":"Result: AC-2 (Reviewer successfully reports findings) is now fully implemented.\n\nDelivered:\n1. **findings/review-findings.md** — Defines the two-stage review findings workflow: (1) Reviewer posts observations as crosslink issue comments with --kind observation, (2) Write-capable agent consolidates observations into structured findings documents. Documents role responsibilities, conventions, and verification steps.\n2. **findings/review-findings-template.md** — Standardized template for review findings documents, including sections for supporting observations (with severity, file:line, source reference), interpreted findings, recommendations, and references.\n3. **findings/README.md** — Updated to include the workflow section linking to review-findings.md, and additional conventions for crosslink issue references and severity levels.\n4. **opencode/agents/reviewer.md** — Added FINDINGS PERSISTENCE section that explains how reviewer observations become durable findings documents, linking to findings/review-findings.md for the full workflow.\n\nThe architecture ensures that:\n- Reviewers (read-only) produce observations via the only channel available to them (crosslink comments)\n- Observations are captured as signed, timestamped, role-identified entries on the hub\n- Findings documents persist the consolidated output for future reference\n- The epistemic pipeline (observation → finding) is preserved","created_at":"2026-07-27T16:31:34.454338994Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:RJCpQiVICYrYCjE2Jbj06Aafa/3iRlGnehHh95MCvIg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAghWuWzCyUk5W6ryufXlYqK7qJNLLR/IGBTS3s1wRZN